@1 = ~Come with me. I could use your help.~
@2 = ~Not just now. Perhaps later.~
@3 = ~Ready when you are.~
@4 = ~Then let's go.~

@10 = ~Caelar's war has driven enough folk from their homes. If ye mean to stop her, ye'll have my hammer.~
@11 = ~Have ye room for an old dwarf again?~
@20 = ~There is a war coming, and Tempus has little use for idle hands. Shall we face it together?~
@21 = ~Are we to fight together again?~
@30 = ~The people fleeing Caelar's army need protection. If you are going north, I would join you.~
@31 = ~Do you need my aid once more?~
@40 = ~Heading for another adventure? I was beginning to tire of this tavern. An able bow might be useful on the road north.~
@41 = ~Room for one more? I promise to make myself useful.~
@50 = ~I've heard enough songs about Sarevok for a lifetime. If you're going after Caelar, I'd rather see the next tale for myself.~
@51 = ~Shall I pack away the lute and come along?~
@60 = ~All these refugees, and half the caravans aren't running. Bad for business. If you're heading north, I could use some work.~
@61 = ~Got work for me again?~
@70 = ~Everyone here looks so miserable. I don't like this talk of war, but perhaps I could help. You might need someone who's good with locks!~
@71 = ~Oh, hello! Are we going adventuring again?~
@80 = ~Another army, another war. I cannot pretend your chances are good, but I can offer my help if you insist on going.~
@81 = ~You have reconsidered? Very well. Our prospects may improve slightly together.~
@90 = ~I have seen what Caelar's army leaves behind. If your road leads against her, our paths may be the same.~
@91 = ~Shall we travel together again?~
@100 = ~So, you are going to fight this Caelar. Better than standing about among soldiers who only talk of it. I could come with you.~
@101 = ~Have you found something worth fighting yet?~
@110 = ~At last! Tiax has endured enough of this cell. Release him, and he shall permit you to accompany him to greater things!~
@111 = ~You return to seek the mighty Tiax's aid. A wise decision!~
